cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: "RLCD: reinforcement learning for calibrated decisions"
abstract: >-
  An agnostic base for training encoder-only models that answer typed questions
  with probability distributions instead of generated text. Training uses a
  strictly proper scoring rule as the reward, so honest probabilities are the
  optimum of the objective. Includes a perturbed-logit policy-gradient trainer,
  held-out temperature calibration, calibration-aware evaluation and an offline
  inference runtime.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Valim
    given-names: Rui
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/ruivalim/rlcd-base"
url: "https://ruivalim.github.io/rlcd-base/"
keywords:
  - calibration
  - decision-making
  - proper scoring rules
  - reinforcement learning
  - encoder-only
  - rlcd
